From: Lasimeri <217267696+Lasimeri@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 14 Sep 2026 20:09:48 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] x86/knc: leave the SBOX I/O APIC unregistered for now

Nothing routes through it yet (the ring devices poll, IPIs use the
LAPIC), its version register reads back 0 through the standard
index/data window, and a boot on 2026-09-14 stopped exactly at that
register read, right after the CPU topology lines. Keep the SFI entries
parsed and skip mp_register_ioapic until the SBOX window is understood;
the registration stays behind CONFIG_KNC_SBOX_IOAPIC, which nothing
defines.
---
 arch/x86/kernel/knc.c | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/x86/kernel/knc.c b/arch/x86/kernel/knc.c
index b230ba38f..fd54133e3 100644
--- a/arch/x86/kernel/knc.c
+++ b/arch/x86/kernel/knc.c
@@ -140,6 +140,14 @@ static void __init knc_parse_smp_config(void)
 	 * SSDG 4.2.5: the I/O APIC pins are SBOX interrupt sources (DMA,
 	 * thermal, doorbells), not ISA IRQs, so no legacy identity mapping.
 	 */
+	/*
+	 * The SBOX I/O APIC is not registered yet: nothing routes through it
+	 * (the ring devices poll, IPIs go through the LAPIC), its version
+	 * register reads back 0 through the standard index/data window, and a
+	 * boot on 2026-09-14 stopped exactly at that register read. It comes
+	 * back once its window is understood; the SFI entries stay parsed.
+	 */
+	if (IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_KNC_SBOX_IOAPIC))
 	for (i = 0; i < knc_sfi.num_ioapics; i++)
 		mp_register_ioapic(i, knc_sfi.ioapic_phys[i], gsi_top, &ioapic_cfg);
 
